---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { scenes } from '../../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ChartGrammar from '../../../components/ChartGrammar.astro';
import AspectDiagram from '../../../components/AspectDiagram.astro';
import { aspects } from '../../../data/aspects';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'Aspects', href: '/explore/aspects/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Aspects. Relationships within the chart" description="Aspects are meaningful angular relationships between planets. Learn conjunctions, sextiles, squares, trines, and oppositions without reducing them to good or bad." path="/explore/aspects/" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
        <h1>Aspects answer: how do chart factors relate?</h1>
        <p class="lede">Aspects are angular relationships between chart factors. They show how different functions meet, reinforce, challenge, interrupt, or complicate one another. This is one of the places where astrology stops being a list and starts becoming a pattern.</p>
      </div>
      <img class="hero__img" src={scenes.aspects.src} srcset={scenes.aspects.srcset} sizes="100vw" alt={scenes.aspects.alt} width={scenes.aspects.width} height={scenes.aspects.height} fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <ChartGrammar active="aspect" />
      <div class="prose flow">
        <h2>See the geometry before naming the story</h2>
        <p>The angle gives the relationship structure. It does not tell us the outcome by itself. Which planets are involved, how exact the aspect is, what those planets rule, and how the person actually lives the pattern all matter.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="aspect-grid">
        {aspects.map((a) => (
          <a class="aspect-card" href={`/explore/aspects/${a.slug}/`}>
            <AspectDiagram name={a.name} degrees={a.degrees} angleLabel={a.angle} />
            <p>{a.nature}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Not simply good or bad</h2>
      <p>I am cautious with the shorthand of "easy" and "hard" aspects. Flow can be underused, friction can become productive, and neither tells you by itself how a person will live a configuration. A square is not a verdict. A trine is not a guarantee.</p>
      <p>When several planets connect through multiple aspects, larger <a href="/explore/chart-patterns/">chart patterns</a> can emerge. Aspects are also central to <a href="/explore/transits/">timing</a>, because moving planets form new relationships to natal chart factors over time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .aspect-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .aspect-card { display: block; padding: var(--space-5); border: 1px solid var(--border-color, currentColor); border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 1rem); text-decoration: none; }
  .aspect-card p { margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; }
  @media (min-width: 700px) { .aspect-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (min-width: 1050px) { .aspect-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
</style>
